+# Scenario: date-fns-utc-now-functions
+
+## Source Issue
+
+`isToday(new UTCDate())` returns `false`, even though a current UTC date should be today.
+
+This is not only an `isToday` edge case. Helpers that compare an input date extension against the current date should construct "now" with the same date constructor as the input where appropriate.
+
+## Constraints
+
+- Fix production source, not the regression test.
+- Do not use the upstream PR patch, oracle commit, or live GitHub.
+- Do not edit package manifests, lockfiles, generated files, or this task file.
+- Do not edit `vitest.config.ts` or any other validation-only configuration.
+- If validation needs cache/output redirection, use the exact command below; do not persist the workaround in repo files.
+- Keep existing Date and timestamp behavior.
+- Prefer the existing local `constructNow` helper where it fits.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run:
+
+```bash
+npx vitest run src/agentflow-realworld-utc-now/test.ts --cache.dir "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/agentflow-vitest-cache-date-fns-utc-now"; status=$?; rm -rf .vitest; exit $status
+```
+
+## Agentflow Output Contract
+
+Write `handoff.md` in `$AGENTFLOW_OUTPUT_DIR` with:
+- a `Scenario` section naming `date-fns-utc-now-functions`
+- a one-sentence issue summary
+- a `Changed files` section with the exact files changed
+- a `Validation` section with the exact command and result
+- a `Risks` section with remaining uncertainty or `none`
